      "code": "ofp_prop = nae->props; props_len = ntohs(nae->len) - offsetof(struct nx_action_encap, props);",
      "note": "Reads the attacker-controlled `nx_action_encap` property slice into typed parser state by setting `ofp_prop = nae->props` and deriving `props_len` from `nae->len`. On the saved witness action this materializes one 8-byte property for the loop to decode.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "lib/ofp-actions.c",
      "function": "decode_NXAST_RAW_ENCAP",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "The function calls `decode_ed_prop(&ofp_prop, out, &props_len)` while keeping `encap` as a raw pointer into `out`, but it never refreshes that pointer after the property loop may grow `out`. The fix saves `encap`'s offset before the loop and reloads it with `ofpbuf_at_assert()` before the later writes.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "lib/ofp-actions.c",
      "function": "decode_NXAST_RAW_ENCAP",
      "line": 4346,
